{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Tradicionál (Anglie)}
{key: Am}
{meta: notation en}

{start_of_verse: label="1."}
[Am]Are you going to [G]Scarborough [Am]Fair?
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[C]ma[D]ry and [Am]thyme;
Re[Am]member [C]me to one [G/B]who [Am]lives [G]there,
[Am]She once [G]was a true love of [Am]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: label="2."}
[Am]Tell her to make me a [G]cambric [Am]shirt,
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[C]ma[D]ry and [Am]thyme,
With[Am]out no [C]seams nor [C]nee-[G/B]ee-[Am]dle [G]work,
[Am]Then she'll [G]be a true love of [Am]mine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: label="3."}
[Am]Tell her to wash it in [G]yonder dry [Am]well,
[C]Parsley, [Am]sage, rose[C]ma[D]ry and [Am]thyme;
Where [Am]never sprung [C]water, nor [C]rain [G/B]ev[Am]er [G]fell,
[Am]And she shall [G]be a true love of [Am]mine.
{end_of_verse}
